parameters.text:
=New booking received.

Call type (event slug): {{ $json.body.payload.type }}
Event title: {{ $json.body.payload.title }}
Start time: {{ $json.body.payload.startTime }}
Client name: {{ $json.body.payload.responses?.name?.value ?? "Not provided" }}
Client email: {{ $json.body.payload.responses?.email?.value ?? "Not provided" }}
What they'd like to discuss: {{ $json.body.payload.responses?.notes?.value ?? $json.body.payload.additionalNotes ?? "No notes provided" }}

Based on this, classify the prep level needed and respond in the required JSON format. And dont mention JSON in the text, just reply in it's syntax.

parameters.inputSchema:
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "call_type": {"type": "string", "enum": ["intro", "strategy", "audit"]},
    "prep_level": {"type": "string", "enum": ["none", "light", "heavy"]},
    "reason": {"type": "string", "description": "one sentence explaining the prep level"},
    "flag_message": {"type": "string", "description": "short Slack-ready message, empty string if prep_level is none"}
  },
  "required": ["call_type", "prep_level", "reason", "flag_message"]
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "subject": {"type": "string", "description": "email subject line for the briefing"},
    "body": {"type": "string", "description": "the full briefing email body text"}
  },
  "required": ["subject", "body"]
}

